From: V <61495413+kelo221@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:36:49 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] NoiseInstance::getAudio: octave weights summing to 0 give
 silence

The output is divided by the sum of the octave weights, so weights that
sum to 0 (all of them 0, or 1 and -1) made every sample infinite or NaN,
which then silenced every voice mixed with it. Such weights now give
silence.
---
 src/audiosource/noise/soloud_noise.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/audiosource/noise/soloud_noise.cpp b/src/audiosource/noise/soloud_noise.cpp
index 7155f59..f3f3a14 100644
--- a/src/audiosource/noise/soloud_noise.cpp
+++ b/src/audiosource/noise/soloud_noise.cpp
@@ -68,7 +68,8 @@ namespace SoLoud
 				}
 				aBuffer[i] += octavevalue[j] * mOctaveScale[j];
 			}
-			aBuffer[i] *= 1.0f/totalscale;
+			// Weights summing to 0 give silence instead of infinity and NaN.
+			aBuffer[i] *= totalscale != 0 ? 1.0f / totalscale : 0.0f;
 		}
 
 		return aSamplesToRead;
